# `client` mode: a headless lobby client that takes a room on BAR's own
# autohosts and runs AI bots in it. The reference for the mode: docker compose
# (env_file), docker run --env-file, or a Kubernetes ConfigMap (rjm.bar.lobbies
# apps/bar-lobbies). Every key and its default is also documented at the top of
# scripts/lobby_client.py. Leave a key out for its default.
#
# The password is NOT here: client.secrets.env.example.

# The account the client logs in as. One session per account: nothing else may
# be logged in as it, Chobby included. It must have accepted BAR's terms once.
BARHOST_LOBBY_LOGIN=CHANGEME

# follow: wait until a user in BARHOST_FOLLOW is in a room, join it as a
# spectator and bring the bots; that user stays boss, starts the game, and can
# PM the client !bots <n> [AI], !join [password], !leave, !status. BAR's
# server does not tell the client who is in other rooms, so the user may have
# to name the room: !room <room number, host, player or title> [password].
# room: take an empty room on BAR's autohosts and run it alone (below). There
# BARHOST_FOLLOW lists the authorised users: they may PM !public, !private,
# !ai [name] [version] (the bots' AI from BARHOST_AI_CHANNELS, a release
# channel optionally held to one release tag; kept across restarts),
# !bots, !stop (resigns the bots by leaving the game), !status,
# !profiler [on|off|default] (the engine profiler from the next game; kept),
# !widgets [on|off|default] (BAR's own widgets in the engine; kept),
# !say <text> (said in the room; a !command is then the boss's), and are made
# boss when they join. In room mode the client ends (!ev) every boss or unboss
# vote an untrusted player calls, and any vote to unboss itself, everyone, or
# a user in this list or BARHOST_AUTO_BOSS. An untrusted player's vote to change
# the start boxes it set (box commands, presets, start settings) is ended too.
BARHOST_CLIENT_MODE=follow
BARHOST_FOLLOW=CHANGEME
BARHOST_LOBBY_HOST=server4.beyondallreason.info
BARHOST_LOBBY_PORT=8200

# Which of BAR's autohost regions to take a room from: a regex on the region of
# Host[EU1], Host[US2], ... Unset = any.
BARHOST_LOBBY_CLUSTER=EU

# room mode only: public (an empty Host[..] room) or private (asked of a region
# manager with !privatehost, as Chobby does; the password is PM'd to the
# BARHOST_FOLLOW users). Only the first start uses this: a BARHOST_FOLLOW user
# can PM !public or !private, and the choice is kept in BARHOST_STATE_FILE.
BARHOST_ROOM_PRIVACY=public
# BARHOST_STATE_FILE=/bar/data/lobby-client-state.json
# room mode: the client is a headless host and spectates. It takes a player
# seat only to be made boss and, briefly, to add bots (BAR's server takes
# ADDBOT only from players), then spectates again.

# room mode only: maps to cycle through, one per game, as the autohost's !map
# takes them (';'-separated; a unique part of a name is enough). Applied once
# boss and after every game; the place is kept in BARHOST_STATE_FILE. A map the
# autohost does not switch to within 20 s, or that cannot be downloaded, is
# skipped. Unset = keep whatever map the room has.
# BARHOST_MAP_ROTATION=All That Glitters;All That Simmers;Hera Planum

# room mode only: start boxes per map, set as boss after every map change
# (the rotation's or a boss's !map) with "!bSet mapmetadata_startbox_override
# <value>", the game's own format, base64url(zlib(json)). The file maps a map
# name (without version) to variants: {"All That Glitters": {"team2_ai": "eNq...",
# "override": "eNq..."}}. The first of BARHOST_START_BOX_KEYS a map has is
# used; a map without one gets "0" (the map's default boxes). Unset = never.
# BARHOST_START_BOXES_FILE=/etc/rjm-bar-host/start-boxes.json
# BARHOST_START_BOX_KEYS=team2_ai,override

# room mode only: said privately in the room to each player who joins (only
# they see it). Unset = no welcome.
# BARHOST_WELCOME=Welcome! The AI bots here run on a server, not a player's PC.

# room mode only: room title (!rename), and the commands sent once boss.
# {bonus} in the title is the AIs' bonus, renamed whenever it changes (e.g.
# "Human vs BARb {bonus}+"). With no human in the player team for a minute
# after someone changed something (a command in the room's chat other than
# !ring, !cv and the like, or a passed vote), the room setup,
# BARHOST_BOT_SETUP, the bot count and the start boxes are applied again:
# anything voted in is undone. At most once every 15 minutes; players joining
# and leaving alone never trigger it.
BARHOST_ROOM_NAME=Co-op vs 8 BARb (Legion on)
BARHOST_ROOM_SETUP=!preset custom;!bSet experimentallegionfaction 1

# The bots (both modes): owned by this client, so its spectating engine runs them. Humans
# play ally team 0; the bots BARHOST_BOT_ALLY. Sides cycle: 0 Armada,
# 1 Cortex, 2 Random (the default, as Chobby adds AIs), 3 Legion. With Legion
# enabled, Random can roll Legion; stock BARb has no Legion configuration
# (SMRTBARb does). Bots are named as Chobby shows them with simple AI names
# off: <AI><BARHOST_BOT_AI_VERSION>(<n>), e.g. BARbstable(1).
# BARHOST_BOT_AI is the AI when BARHOST_AI_CHANNELS is unset.
BARHOST_BOT_AI=BARb
BARHOST_BOT_COUNT=8
BARHOST_BOT_ALLY=1
BARHOST_BOT_SIDES=2
BARHOST_BOT_AI_VERSION=stable
# BARHOST_BOT_PROFILE={"profile":"hard"}
# Chat commands (';'-separated) sent each time after the client adds bots, for
# settings that apply to the AIs present, e.g. every AI's resource bonus.
# BARHOST_BOT_SETUP=!setallaibonus 50

# room mode only: a friend request to each player who joins the room, once per
# account (kept in BARHOST_STATE_FILE). 0 (default) or 1.
# BARHOST_FRIEND_JOINERS=0
# Friend list upkeep (any mode). BAR's lobby server counts friends plus pending
# requests both ways against one limit (300 by default), and refuses new
# requests once it is reached. Every 6 h (and a minute after login) the client
# reads the list: requests not accepted within PENDING_DAYS are withdrawn, and
# friends it has not seen online for OFFLINE_DAYS are removed, never a
# BARHOST_FOLLOW or BARHOST_AUTO_BOSS user. The server does not say when
# someone was last online, so that count starts when the client last saw them
# (or when it first listed them). While the server says the list is full,
# no requests for 6 h; refused players are asked again later. 0 = never.
# BARHOST_FRIEND_PENDING_DAYS=0
# BARHOST_FRIEND_OFFLINE_DAYS=0

# room mode only: the client never starts a game. Once this many humans are
# in, ready and synced, it says how to vote the start (!cv start); 0 = never.
# No hint for BARHOST_POSTGAME_DELAY seconds after a game.
BARHOST_MIN_HUMANS=1
# room mode only: 1 = also wait until at least as many humans play as there
# are bots in the room (teams matched in size); 0 = the default, off.
BARHOST_MATCHED_TEAMS=0
# room mode only: once at least as many humans play as there are bots and
# someone is not ready, say `!ring` (the autohost rings every unready player)
# BARHOST_RING_FIRST seconds later, then every BARHOST_RING_EVERY, also in the
# post-game delay; 0 = never, the default.
BARHOST_RING_EVERY=0
BARHOST_RING_FIRST=15
# room mode only: 1 = say `!balance` once the room is set up (after the bots,
# so their team ids are fixed) and each time the player team fills (as many
# humans as bots, or the room full), at most once every 30 s, also in the
# post-game delay; 0 = never, the default.
BARHOST_BALANCE=0
# room mode only: 1 = the players vote the AI bonus through the client, since
# SPADS lets no non-boss vote it while the client is boss: a player says
# `aibonus <0-100>`, the players say y or n within 60 s, and a majority (or
# more yes than no at the end) applies !setallaibonus. The word "bonus" and
# the end of every game (once the next map is in) get the how-to. Each player
# may call one every BARHOST_BONUS_VOTE_COOLDOWN seconds. 0 = off, the default.
BARHOST_BONUS_VOTE=0
BARHOST_BONUS_VOTE_COOLDOWN=300
BARHOST_POSTGAME_DELAY=60

# room mode only: a player seat while fewer than BARHOST_BOOST_BELOW humans
# play, so the battle list shows the room busier (0 = never, the default); a
# spectator again from BARHOST_BOOST_UNTIL humans or a full room, once
# everyone is ready, and when a start is called. In between, the seat is kept.
# room mode only: trusted players (','-separated, exact case) made boss when
# they join, as BARHOST_FOLLOW users are. Lobby boss only: they cannot PM the
# client commands.
# BARHOST_AUTO_BOSS=

# BARHOST_BOOST_BELOW=0
# BARHOST_BOOST_UNTIL=7

# room mode only: PM the autohost !promote (it advertises the room in #main)
# while a public room has fewer humans than bots (no bots: a free seat), no
# game runs and no start is near: once the room is set up, as soon as a game
# is over, and this many seconds apart: BAR's autohosts allow one every 600
# (promoteDelay). Its "Please wait ..." answer sets the next try. 0 = never.
# BARHOST_PROMOTE_EVERY=0

# Content fetched at start, so joining a room needs at most a small update. The
# client downloads whatever game and map the room uses when it joins.
BARHOST_GAMETYPE=byar:test
BARHOST_MAPS=All That Glitters v2.2.3

# A custom AI from a GitHub release, installed at start (then allow it with
# BARHOST_BOT_AI). Stock BARb needs nothing. On a moving tag (@latest: newest
# non-pre-release; @newest: including pre-releases) the client also installs
# a new release between games: after every game, and every
# BARHOST_AI_UPDATE_EVERY seconds while no game runs (0 = never).
# BARHOST_AI_ARCHIVES=github:S3KCentrifugal/CircuitAI@newest
BARHOST_AI_UPDATE_EVERY=900

# AI channels: the AIs an authorised user picks with !ai <name> (by PM; !ai
# alone lists them), kept across restarts. Each is name=AI (the engine's own
# AI, e.g. stock BARb) or name=AI:github:OWNER/REPO@TAG[#GLOB] (a release).
# Every channel's release is downloaded at start and checked between games
# (as above), into BARHOST_AI_RELEASES_DIR (put it on a volume, so releases
# survive restarts); the engine is pointed at the chosen one between games.
# Releases of one AI (test and prod builds, both SMRTBARb) are swapped without
# touching the bots; another AI's name replaces the bots. !ai <name> <tag>
# holds a release channel to that release (e.g. !ai smrt-test v1.1150-test)
# until !ai <name> again; the asset GLOB still picks the file. BARHOST_AI_CHANNEL
# is the channel until one is picked (default: the first). Replaces
# BARHOST_BOT_AI and BARHOST_AI_ARCHIVES for the bots.
# BARHOST_AI_CHANNELS=barb=BARb;smrt-prod=SMRTBARb:github:S3KCentrifugal/CircuitAI@latest;smrt-test=SMRTBARb:github:S3KCentrifugal/CircuitAI@newest#*-test-linux.tar.gz
# BARHOST_AI_CHANNEL=smrt-prod
# BARHOST_AI_RELEASES_DIR=/bar/data/ai-releases

# Per-game diagnostics and the game archive. Each game runs in its own engine
# write dir under BARHOST_WORK_DIR: put it on fast storage (an SSD), because
# the engine writes its logs there line by line during the game. Every
# BARHOST_METRICS_EVERY seconds (0 = off) a widget in the engine logs how far
# it is behind the server (LuaUI/Config/rjm-engine-timeline.csv in the write
# dir: BAR lets user widgets write only there) and the client logs the
# engine's CPU per thread, memory, disk and the container's pressure
# (timeline.csv, threads.csv). BARHOST_ENGINE_PROFILER=1 also turns the engine
# profiler on and records every engine timer's time per interval
# (rjm-engine-profile.csv: "Sim", "AI", "Sim::Path", ...; its own cost is the
# timer Misc::Profiler::AddTime). A BARHOST_FOLLOW user's PM `!profiler on|off`
# overrides it from the next game, kept in BARHOST_STATE_FILE until
# `!profiler default`.
# After the engine exits, the game (replay, metrics, logs, lobby data) is
# moved into BARHOST_ARCHIVE_DIR by a low-priority process (game_archive.py:
# the layout is in its docstring), named BARHOST_ARCHIVE_SOURCE (the login);
# unset, it stays in the work dir. One archive can take games from many
# clients and pods.
# BARHOST_WORK_DIR=/bar/work
# BARHOST_ARCHIVE_DIR=/bar/archive
# BARHOST_ARCHIVE_SOURCE=bar-lobbies.clyde
# Chat audit log, appended as it happens (UTC):
#   private/YYYY-MM-DD.log   every private message, both ways, every sender;
#                            "<- user [authorised|autohost|not authorised,
#                            ignored]: text", "-> user: text"
#   rooms/YYYY/MM/DD/<joined>Z_room<id>.log   one room session: chat, joins,
#                            leaves, the client's own messages, game start/over
#   channels/YYYY-MM-DD.log  lobby channel chat, if any
# Default: BARHOST_ARCHIVE_DIR/_chat/BARHOST_ARCHIVE_SOURCE; none without either.
# BARHOST_CHAT_DIR=/bar/archive/_chat/bar-lobbies.clyde
# BARHOST_METRICS_EVERY=5
# A game standing still (its frame unchanged in the metrics widget's timeline
# while the engine runs: paused, with every player resigned or gone, never
# reaches game over) is given up after BARHOST_FROZEN_GAME_MINUTES once every
# human who started has resigned or left it (the engine's console), or after 6
# times that regardless: the bots resign and the client moves to a new room.
# A lagging engine's frame still moves, so lag never counts. Needs
# BARHOST_METRICS_EVERY. 0 (default) = never.
# BARHOST_FROZEN_GAME_MINUTES=0
# BARHOST_ENGINE_PROFILER=0
# 0 (default) = BAR's own widgets off in games: only the metrics widget, BAR's Autoquit
# (it quits the engine after game over) and BAR's hidden helpers load, from a LuaUI/Config/BYAR.lua the client writes with every
# widget name learnt from earlier games at order 0. A headless engine runs
# every widget's Lua on the sim thread. A BARHOST_FOLLOW user's PM
# `!widgets on|off` overrides it from the next game, kept until
# `!widgets default`.
# BARHOST_BAR_WIDGETS=0
# BARHOST_WIDGET_NAMES_FILE=/bar/data/bar-widget-names.json (next to BARHOST_STATE_FILE)
